    "title": "Kevin McGonigle, Tarik Skubal lead Detroit Tigers on Opening Day",
    "text": "TIGERSKevin McGonigle leads Tigers in 8-2 win over Padres on Opening Day Evan PetzoldDetroit Free PressMarch 26, 2026Updated March 27, 2026, 5:25 a.m. ETSubscribe to hear this storySAN DIEGO – Detroit Tigers top prospect Kevin McGonigle thought he would feel nervous for the first pitch of his MLB debut, then settle in.But McGonigle didn't seem nervous.He looked like he belonged.On Opening Day, McGonigle pulled the first pitch he saw – an up-and-in cutter from right-hander Nick Pivetta – into right field for a two-run double in the first inning. The first hit of McGonigle's career paved the way for an 8-2 win over the San Diego Padres on Thursday, March 26, at Petco Park.If you purchase through our links, the USA Today Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
